# Security response headers. Cloudflare Workers Static Assets applies this file to every
# STATIC response (every prerendered page, /studio/, and /_astro/* files). It does NOT
# apply to responses the Worker generates itself: /preview/**, /preview/live and
# /api/draft-mode/* are SSR routes and carry none of these headers (checked 2026-09-29
# against production: /preview/ answers with no CSP at all). See "What is not covered".
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Content-Security-Policy (full policy since 2026-09-29, tier-2 hardening)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two policies, scoped by path, so the public site does not carry the Studio's grants:
#
#   /*          the public site. Tight: nothing loads from anywhere this site does not
#               actually use.
#   /studio/*   the embedded Sanity Studio. Detaches the public policy with
#               "! Content-Security-Policy" and sets its own. The detach is required:
#               Cloudflare MERGES the headers of every matching rule, and two CSP
#               headers are both enforced (the browser takes the intersection), so
#               without it the Studio would still be held to the public policy.
#   /_astro/*   hashed JS/CSS. The CSP is detached here because a Web Worker is
#               governed by the policy on ITS OWN script response, not the page's.
#               Any worker the Studio starts from /_astro/ would otherwise be held to
#               the public policy (no Sanity hosts) and fail silently. JS and CSS
#               files are not documents, so nothing else reads a CSP on them.
#               THIS RULE ALSO OWNS THE IMMUTABLE CACHE-CONTROL. @astrojs/cloudflare
#               normally prepends its own `/_astro/*` block at build, but two rules
#               with the same path did not merge under wrangler dev: the adapter's
#               rule plus a detach-only rule here silently dropped the year-long cache on every hashed asset
#               (seen under `npm run preview`, 2026-09-29). With Cache-Control set
#               here the adapter sees it and skips its injection ("_headers already
#               sets Cache-Control on a matching rule"), so there is one rule.
#
# Every origin below is used by something in src/. Inventory (2026-09-29):
#   script-src  www.googletagmanager.com   GA4 gtag.js (src/components/analytics/GoogleAnalytics.astro)
#               static.cloudflareinsights.com  Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon, when
#                                          PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN is set (CloudflareBeacon.astro)
#               'unsafe-inline'            unavoidable on a static build with no per-request
#                                          nonce: the anti-FOUC theme script, the GA stub,
#                                          Astro's island loader, and ClientRouter all run inline.
#                                          (A hash-based `security.csp` was tried and broke
#                                          the site; see docs/agent/stack-and-config.md.)
#   connect-src api.web3forms.com          contact form (ContactForm.tsx). The newsletter signup
#                                          that also posted here was removed 2026-09-30; it
#                                          never used any other origin, so nothing else went.
#               *.google-analytics.com, *.analytics.google.com, www.googletagmanager.com,
#               *.g.doubleclick.net, www.google.com   GA4 collection (Google's published CSP
#                                          list). www.google.com/g/collect is NOT optional: this
#                                          property sends every hit there too (Google signals),
#                                          and the 2026-09-29 sweep caught it blocked on every
#                                          page before it was added. Visitors routed to a
#                                          country Google domain (google.co.uk etc.) will have
#                                          that one ads-signal request blocked; GA4 itself
#                                          still records the hit via google-analytics.com.
#               cloudflareinsights.com     the beacon's RUM POST
#               ba403vjc.api(cdn).sanity.io  no public page reads Sanity from the browser
#                                          today; allowed for our own project only so a
#                                          future client-side read does not fail silently
#               'wasm-unsafe-eval'         Pagefind site search at /search compiles its same-origin
#                                          WebAssembly (/pagefind/); without it /search loads and
#                                          then fails to start. It permits compiling WASM only,
#                                          not eval() of JavaScript.
#   frame-src   calendly.com               click-to-load scheduler (CalendlyInline.tsx)
#               www.youtube.com, www.youtube-nocookie.com, player.vimeo.com
#                                          VideoEmbed section
#               www.google.com             ServiceAreaMap.astro (the Google map embed on /contact;
#                                          www.openstreetmap.org until 2026-10-01)
#   img-src     https:                     Sanity CDN photos, GA's pixel. (It was broad for the
#                                          shop's affiliate images from arbitrary retailers; the
#                                          shop went 2026-09-30, so this could now be narrowed.
#                                          Left as-is on purpose: a separate, tested change.)
#   font-src    'self'                     all three families are self-hosted via @fontsource
#   form-action api.web3forms.com          the no-JS fallback path of the contact form
#
# ADDING AN EMBED OR A THIRD PARTY: add its origin to the right directive HERE, on the
# right policy, and check it under `npm run preview` (a static file server sends no
# headers, so it cannot show a CSP problem). A blocked request never leaves the browser,
# so no server log will ever show it: the only evidence is a console line reading
# "violates the following Content-Security-Policy directive".
#
# The Studio grants are the ones in the vault gotcha
# _vault/gotchas/embedded-studio-blocked-by-your-own-csp.md (presacademy is the
# reference): Sanity API + live websocket + sanity-cdn.com version ping in connect-src,
# design-system-static.sanity.io in font-src, blob: workers.
#
# NO upgrade-insecure-requests, on purpose. It was in the first draft and it broke
# `npm run preview`: a link to /about answers 307 -> http://127.0.0.1:4342/about/, the
# directive rewrote that to https://, and the click navigation silently died. In
# production it buys nothing: HSTS already forces https, and img-src/media-src only
# allow https: anyway.
#
# What is not covered: /preview/** (see the top of this file). Giving it a policy means
# setting the header from the SSR code, not from here. Tracked in docs/PENDING.md.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# frame-ancestors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Replaces the legacy X-Frame-Options so a Studio can iframe this site for preview.
# 'self' is the entry that matters: the Studio is EMBEDDED at /studio on this same
# origin, so the Presentation tool's iframe of /preview/* is a same-origin frame. The
# sanity.io entries stay: Sanity's own hosted tooling can still frame the site.
# (2026-09-05: the retired reid-design.sanity.studio and localhost:3333/3334 entries
# were removed.)

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self' https://www.sanity.io https://*.sanity.io; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' https:; font-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.web3forms.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.g.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://ba403vjc.api.sanity.io https://ba403vjc.apicdn.sanity.io; frame-src 'self' https://calendly.com https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com https://www.google.com; form-action 'self' https://api.web3forms.com; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

/studio/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self' data: https://design-system-static.sanity.io; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self' https://api.sanity.io https://*.api.sanity.io wss://*.api.sanity.io https://*.apicdn.sanity.io https://cdn.sanity.io https://sanity-cdn.com https://*.sanity-cdn.com; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com; form-action 'self' https://api.sanity.io https://*.api.sanity.io; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'

/_astro/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
